---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const seo = {
  title: "Track Zerodha and Groww Portfolio Together (Without Sharing Passwords) | Arthavi",
  description: "Learn how to view your Zerodha stocks and Groww mutual funds in a single dashboard. A secure, privacy-first guide for Indian investors using Arthavi.",
};
---
<Layout
  title={seo.title}
  description={seo.description}
  keywords="track zerodha and groww together, zerodha groww portfolio consolidation, best app to track stocks and mutual funds india, portfolio tracker for multiple brokers, arthavi vs indmoney"
  schema={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Article",
    "headline": "Track Zerodha and Groww Portfolio Together (Without Sharing Passwords)",
    "image": "https://arthavi.com/images/og-image.png",
    "author": {
      "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "Arthavi"
      },
      "publisher": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "Arthavi",
        "logo": {
          "@type": "ImageObject",
          "url": "https://arthavi.com/images/logo.png"
        }
      },
      "datePublished": "2026-02-16",
      "description": "A guide on consolidating Zerodha and Groww portfolios into one dashboard securely."
    })}
  breadcrumb={{
    items: [
      { name: "Home", url: "https://arthavi.com/" },
      { name: "Blog", url: "https://arthavi.com/blog/track-zerodha-groww-portfolio-together" }
    ]
  }}
>

    

    <main class="container" style="padding-top: calc(var(--header-height) + 2rem);">
        <article class="prose fade-in" style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">
            <h1 style="font-size: 2.5rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Track Zerodha and Groww Portfolio Together (Without
                Sharing Passwords)</h1>

            <p style="font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 2rem;">
                The classic Indian investor dilemma: You perform your stock trading on <strong><a href="/arthavi-vs-zerodha/">Zerodha Kite</a></strong>
                because of its clean UI, but you started your SIPs on <strong><a href="/arthavi-vs-groww/">Groww</a></strong> because it was easy to set
                up.
            </p>

            <p>Now, you have a fragmented net worth. You have to open two apps, check two different totals, and mentally
                add them up to know how rich (or poor) you are today.</p>

            <div
                style="margin: 3rem 0; padding: 2rem; background: var(--bg-surface); border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05);">
                <h2 style="margin-top: 0;">The Problem with "Just Use One App"</h2>
                <p>Moving your entire portfolio is a hassle. It involves:</p>
                <ul style="margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li>Closing a Demat account (painful paperwork).</li>
                    <li>Stopping and restarting SIPs (losing track of vintage).</li>
                    <li>Paying capital gains tax if you sell and rebuy.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="margin-top: 1rem;">It's smarter to keep your brokers as they are and use a <strong>unified
                        layer</strong> on top.</p>
            </div>

            <h2>Why Most "Unified" Apps Are Dangerous</h2>
            <p>Many popular apps (we won't name them) offer to "sync" your Zerodha and Groww accounts. They do this by
                asking for:</p>
            <ol>
                <li>Your broker username/password (Huge security risk!).</li>
                <li>Your email access to read contract notes (Privacy risk!).</li>
                <li>Your SMS permissions to read transaction alerts.</li>
            </ol>
            <p><strong>This is a bad trade.</strong> You are giving away the keys to your financial kingdom just to see
                a pie chart.</p>

            <div class="glass-panel" style="margin: 3rem 0; padding: 2.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--primary-glow);">
                <h2 style="margin-top: 0; color: var(--primary-glow);">The Safe Solution: Arthavi</h2>
                <p>Arthavi allows you to track Zerodha (Stocks) and Groww (Mutual Funds) together <strong>without
                        linking your accounts</strong>.</p>

                <h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">How It Works:</h3>

                <h4 style="color: var(--text-head); margin-bottom: 0.5rem; margin-top: 1.5rem;">For Groww (Mutual
                    Funds):</h4>
                <p>Groww stores your mutual fund units with a central depository (CAMS/KFintech). You simply download
                    your <strong>Consolidated Account Statement (CAS)</strong> and upload it to Arthavi. We parse the
                    PDF locally.</p>

                <h4 style="color: var(--text-head); margin-bottom: 0.5rem; margin-top: 1.5rem;">For Zerodha (Stocks):
                </h4>
                <p>You can export your holdings from Zerodha Console as a CSV/Excel file. Upload this file to Arthavi's
                    "Import Stocks" feature. We will map the ISINs to real-time prices.</p>

                <div style="margin-top: 2rem; text-align: center;">
                    <a href="https://app.arthavi.com" class="btn btn-primary">Consolidate My Portfolio Free</a>
                </div>
            </div>

            <h2>Benefits of a Consolidated View</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>True Net Worth:</strong> See the sum of Stocks + Mutual Funds + Cash in one number.</li>
                <li><strong>Asset Allocation:</strong> Realize that you are actually 80% exposed to equity when you
                    thought you were balanced.</li>
                <li><strong>Overlap Check:</strong> Discover that your "Diversified Equity Fund" holds the same HDFC
                    Bank shares that you bought directly on Zerodha.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Step-by-Step Guide</h2>
            <ol>
                <li><strong>Login to Arthavi:</strong> Create a <a href="https://app.arthavi.com">free account</a>.</li>
                <li><strong>Import Mutual Funds:</strong> Use the "Import Investments" feature (See our <a
                        href="/blog/how-to-download-analyze-cams-cas-statement/">guide on downloading your investment statement</a>).</li>
                <li><strong>Import Stocks:</strong> Go to Zerodha Console > Portfolio > Holdings > Download CSV. Upload
                    this to Arthavi.</li>
                <li><strong>Done!</strong> Your unified dashboard is ready.</li>
            </ol>

            <p>Stop toggling apps. Start tracking wealth.</p>

        </article>
    </main>

</Layout>
